<title>PORTUGAL: Portucel loses 1.4 bln esc in 1996.</title>
<headline>Portucel loses 1.4 bln esc in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net loss		 1.37     vs    18.14 profit</p>
<p>    Gross dividend	 17.5 escudos  vs    45 escudos</p>
<p>    Turnover		     46.85     vs    70.54</p>
<p>    Operating loss		0.55     vs    19.80 profit</p>
<p>    Cash-flow		     5.27     vs    25.13</p>
<p>    Net debt		     12.10     vs    14.20</p>
<p>Note - Portucel Industrial-Empresa Produtora de Celulose is full company name.  </p>
<p>The company said the second quarter of 1996, when it lost 2.95 billion escudos, had been particularly difficult. It moved back into the black in the last two quarters with profits of 213 million and 1.36 billion escudos, respectively.</p>
<p>The losses for 1996 were at the lower end of analysts' forecasts.</p>
<p>The company said that it had succeeded in containing costs in 1996.</p>
<p>Production costs fell 10 percent compared with 1995, while variable unit costs fell 13 percent for white pulp. Staff costs dropped six percent.</p>
<p>($1=168.2 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
